<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy — JobsOxo"
  description="What information JobsOxo collects on jobsoxo.com and through the waitlist, and what we do with it."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  effective="[Month Day, 2026]"
>
  <p>
    JobsOxo, LLC (“JobsOxo,” “we,” “us”) is based in New York, NY. This policy explains what information we collect on
    jobsoxo.com and through our waitlist, and what we do with it. Short version: we collect only what we need to let you
    in, we never sell it, and you can ask us to delete it any time.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
    <p>When you join the waitlist: your <strong>name, email address, type of work and crew size</strong>.</p>
    <p>
      When you visit the site: basic technical information such as browser type, device, pages viewed and approximate
      location (city/country), collected through Plausible Analytics. Plausible doesn’t use cookies or track you across
      other websites, and we do not use advertising cookies.
    </p>
    <p>
      We also use Google Analytics to understand how people find and use the site. Google Analytics sets cookies and
      collects similar technical information, including an identifier for your browser. You can opt out with Google’s
      browser add-on at <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.
    </p>
    <p>When you email us: your email address.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To contact you when your waitlist spot opens and to set up your account.</li>
      <li>To send occasional product updates about JobsOxo. You can unsubscribe from any email.</li>
      <li>To understand who’s signing up so we build the right features.</li>
      <li>To keep the site secure and working.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell or rent your information. We share it only with service providers that help us run JobsOxo, and
      only for that purpose: Vercel (hosting), Supabase (database), Resend (email), and Plausible and Google Analytics
      (analytics). We may also disclose information if required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep waitlist information until you ask us to delete it, or until 12 months after our last contact with you if
      you never create an account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask to see, correct or delete your information at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:hello@jobsoxo.com"
        >hello@jobsoxo.com</a
      >. We’ll respond within 30 days. Depending on where you live (for example, California), you may have additional
      rights under local law, and we’ll honor them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reputable providers, encrypted connections (HTTPS) and limited access to protect your information. No
      system is perfectly secure, but we take reasonable steps to keep your data safe and will tell you promptly if
      there’s a breach that affects you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Children</h2>
    <p>JobsOxo is for businesses. We don’t knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we’ll update the date at the top. If the change is significant, we’ll email you first.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      JobsOxo, LLC · [Mailing address], New York, NY · <a href="mailto:hello@jobsoxo.com">hello@jobsoxo.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
